Whilst we're proposing new features:

I was playing a Barbarian on Saturday and got to thinking:  a floating eye
gives telepathy, and the message talks about one's "mental acuity".  So why
does telepathy work even if you don't have much of a mental state to begin
with?

Specifically, if the character's intelligence is below some level, telepathy
should include an effect like hallucination:  you know it's there, you just
don't know what it is.  Dumber, and some of the smaller (i.e. stupider, for
telepathy?) and/or farther away monsters don't even show up.  Still dumber,
and this starts to happen close up as well.

Unfortunately, my ruminations were then interrupted as NetHack proceeded to
blow up with an illegal instruction; d*mned if I know why at present, but I
did remove the setuid from it so I'll have a core dump to examine next time.
